257-## Reusable knowledge
--
259-- The working artifact is `apps/music-plugins/audio-tools/sfx-design-study/`: human entry `index.html`, canonical notes `PROJECT_NOTES.md`, and numeric design `design/TOKEN_SHEET.md`. Compare A「音のしぐさを移す」, B「ありえない素材を触る」, and C「音を会話させる」; the initial prototype uses independent timbre and temporal gesture (volume, pitch, gaps, repetition). Synplant, GameSynth, Patatap, and W3C APG Radio were official-reference inputs, but no hands-on use/listening was verified. [Task 1]
260-- `sfx-engine.js?v=6` must expose `EDIT_LIMITS`, `renderEdited`, and `createLivePlayer`; if the required engine is old or fails to load, disable playback, mutation, editing, and reset and show reload guidance (fail closed). C editing is deliberately isolated: gaps change `time` only, pitch flow changes `semitone` only, and tail changes final `length` only; preserve all unrelated event values and timbre assignments across nine base sounds. [Task 2]
261:- Final QA covered 99 combinations (3 timbres × 3 gestures × 11 settings): peak 0.205–0.379, RMS 0.0149–0.0401, A-return difference `4.47e-08`, console errors 0, and no horizontal overflow at 1440/390/320px. `design-lint` recorded NG 0, WARN 0, and measurement-unavailable 0. P1–P3 set values and play C in one press; manual changes clear the preset indication; blur, stop, and reset were checked. [Task 2]
